#: ../../../prop_tgt/EMBT_RUNTIME_LIBRARY.rst:2
msgid "EMBT_RUNTIME_LIBRARY"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prop_tgt/EMBT_RUNTIME_LIBRARY.rst:6
msgid ""
"Select the runtime library used by the Embarcadero (``bcc64x``) toolchain."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prop_tgt/EMBT_RUNTIME_LIBRARY.rst:8
msgid "The allowed values are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prop_tgt/include/EMBT_RUNTIME_LIBRARY-VALUES.rst:1
msgid "``Static``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prop_tgt/include/EMBT_RUNTIME_LIBRARY-VALUES.rst:2
msgid ""
"Compile without additional flags to use the statically-linked runtime "
"library."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prop_tgt/include/EMBT_RUNTIME_LIBRARY-VALUES.rst:4
msgid "``Dynamic``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prop_tgt/include/EMBT_RUNTIME_LIBRARY-VALUES.rst:5
msgid ""
"Compile with ``-tR`` and define ``USEPACKAGES`` to use the dynamically-"
"linked (shared) runtime library."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prop_tgt/include/EMBT_RUNTIME_LIBRARY-VALUES.rst:8
msgid ""
"The value is ignored on non-Embarcadero compilers but an unsupported value "
"will be rejected as an error when using the ``bcc64x`` toolchain."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prop_tgt/include/EMBT_RUNTIME_LIBRARY-VALUES.rst:11
msgid ""
"If this property is not set then no runtime library selection flag is added "
"explicitly by CMake, which is equivalent to ``Static``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prop_tgt/EMBT_RUNTIME_LIBRARY.rst:12
msgid ""
"Use :manual:`generator expressions <cmake-generator-expressions(7)>` to "
"support per-configuration specification."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prop_tgt/EMBT_RUNTIME_LIBRARY.rst:15
msgid "For example, the code:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prop_tgt/EMBT_RUNTIME_LIBRARY.rst:17
msgid ""
"add_library(mylib SHARED mylib.cxx)\n"
"set_property(TARGET mylib PROPERTY EMBT_RUNTIME_LIBRARY \"Dynamic\")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prop_tgt/EMBT_RUNTIME_LIBRARY.rst:22
msgid ""
"selects for the target ``mylib`` the dynamically-linked runtime library."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prop_tgt/EMBT_RUNTIME_LIBRARY.rst:24
msgid ""
"This property is initialized by the :variable:`CMAKE_EMBT_RUNTIME_LIBRARY` "
"variable if it is set when a target is created.  It has no effect on "
"toolchains other than ``EMBTClang``."
msgstr ""
